.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ttychatter.python
is the full line-oriented Bash client with Python 3 helpers for JSON, attachment,
log, export, streaming, branch, and edit-turn operations. It is intended to stay
closer to the C command-line edition than the Bash-only or ncurses editions.
.SH SESSION LOGS AND TITLES
New logs begin with the shared pre-chat line:
.PP
.nf
Everyone is encouraged to get the cruelty-free vegetarian alternatives and remember the bloodguilt curse from the Bible... http://bloodguiltcurse.net
.fi
.PP
Unnamed logs initially use timestamped filenames. Interactive new or unnamed
sessions prominently ask for a name when PROMPT_SESSION_NAME=1 (the default).
Enter defers naming. Piped input and batch prompts are never consumed for a name.
.PP
Naming with :rename or --rename-session changes both session-title metadata and
the actual filename to TITLE--ID.log. TITLE is a safe, at most 80-character ASCII
slug; ID is the first 12 characters of a separate stable 32-character session ID.
A numeric suffix resolves collisions without replacing another file.
Manual titles preserve up to 200 characters and are not limited by the automatic
title word limit. Existing timestamped and explicitly named logs still open.
The client reports the current log path after every generation attempt.
.PP
The current human title and recorded previous titles or filename stems can be
used to resume, export, or manage a renamed session. An exact existing filename
takes priority. If a title or alias matches multiple logs, choose the filename
shown by --list. Alias searches only inspect regular, nonsymlink session logs.
.PP
--output FILE remains the chosen path during naming prompts and automatic title
generation. An explicit :rename or --rename-session can rename it in place.
Symbolic-link logs are not renamed. Log renaming needs ln with -T support and a
filesystem that supports hard links; an unsupported rename leaves the original.
New logs are private to the current user.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.TP
.B --demo
Use local demo responses and demo model metadata.
.TP
.BR -i , " --interactive"
Force interactive mode even when stdin is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR -n , " --new"
Create a fresh timestamped session.
.TP
.BR -p , " --prompt " TEXT
Send TEXT once.
.TP
.BR --input " FILE"
Read one-shot prompt text from FILE. Use - for stdin.
.TP
.BR -o , " --output " FILE
Use FILE as the session log path for the invocation.
.TP
.BR -s , " --session " SESSION
Use a named session or .log path.
.TP
.B --resume SESSION
Resume an existing session.
.TP
.B --list
List saved sessions with metadata titles.
.TP
.B --sessions
Alias for --list.
.TP
.BR --rename-session " SESSION TITLE"
Set the friendly title and safely rename the actual log file.
.TP
.BR --search " QUERY"
Search session logs. Use --all-sessions to search every saved log.
.TP
.BR --turns " SESSION"
List user/assistant message numbers.
.TP
.BR --branch " SESSION TURN"
Create an independently identified, named branch after TURN.
.TP
.BR --edit-turn " SESSION TURN"
Open a user turn in the external editor, create a branch, and continue from the edited prompt.
.TP
.BR --export " SESSION"
Export a session in markdown, text, or json.
Multiline messages and code fences are preserved; internal metadata is omitted.
An output-file write failure returns a nonzero status.
.TP
.BR --format " markdown|text|json"
Choose export format.
.TP
.B --models
List models. Supports --all, --model-type, --sort, --min-input-tokens,
--min-output-tokens, --require-tokens, --allow-missing-tokens, --show-preview, and --hide-preview.
.TP
.B --routers
Alias for --models --model-type routers.
.TP
.B --update-models
Refresh model cache.
.TP
.B --autoscan-model
Removed compatibility flag. Prints guidance toward --models, --select-model, and --test-model.
.TP
.B --test-model MODEL
Test one model. Use --save to persist a successful choice.
.TP
.B --select-model
Open a numbered model selector. Use --save to persist.
.TP
.B --favorites
List favorite models.
.TP
.B --favorite-model MODEL
Bookmark MODEL.
.TP
.B --unfavorite-model MODEL
Remove MODEL from favorites. --unbookmark-model is also accepted.
.TP
.B --set-api-key
Prompt for an API key and offer runtime-only, gpg-encrypted, or plaintext config storage.
.TP
.B --forget-api-key
Remove plaintext key config.
.TP
.B --config
Print config summary.
.TP
.BR --set " KEY VALUE"
Save config.
.TP
.BR --unset " KEY"
Remove config.
.TP
.BR --show-memory , " --edit-memory" , " --clear-memory " SESSION
Inspect or modify stored context snapshots.
.TP
.B --editor-prompt
Compose a prompt in VISUAL, EDITOR, nano, or vi.
.TP
.BR --attach " FILE"
Attach FILE to the next request.
.TP
.BR --stream , " --no-stream"
Stream provider token deltas while still saving the final complete response. Press ESC during an active stream to stop it; the partial reply is saved with an interruption marker.
.TP
.BR --web , " --no-web"
Enable or disable the OpenRouter web-search server tool. The default is off.
The model decides when to search. Sources are appended to the answer and log.
.TP
.BR --web-engine " ENGINE"
Select auto, native, exa, parallel, perplexity, or firecrawl. Default: auto.
.TP
.BR --web-max-results " N"
Set results per search, from 0 to 25 (default 5). Zero leaves the provider default. Perplexity is capped at 20 when nonzero.
.TP
.BR --web-max-uses " N"
Set search rounds from 0 to 25 (default 3). Zero omits ttychatter's max_tool_calls cap.
.TP
.BR --ai-download " ask|auto|metadata|off"
Control provider-returned file attachments. The default ask mode prompts before saving when a terminal can answer and records metadata only in noninteractive use. auto saves all returned files under ATTACHMENT_DIR/received, metadata lists them without saving, and off ignores them.
.TP
.BR --status , " --progress"
Show local progress/status notes. These are not hidden model thoughts.
.TP
.BR --no-status , " --no-progress"
Disable status/progress notes.
.TP
.BR --voice-input " FILE"
Transcribe FILE with VOICE_INPUT_CMD and send it.
.TP
.BR --transcribe " FILE"
Print transcription from VOICE_INPUT_CMD.
.TP
.BR --speak , " --no-speak"
Enable or disable assistant-output TTS using VOICE_OUTPUT_CMD or TTS_CMD.
.TP
.B --loopback
Route interface text to stderr and model output to stdout.
.TP
.BR --loopback-file " PATH"
Append each model output to PATH.
.TP
.B --doctor
Run diagnostics.
.TP
.B --credits
Show credits.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The shared config file is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/config
or, when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset,
.IR ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config .
Sessions default to
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions ,
attachments to
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments ,
and the model cache to
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json .
Model favorites default to
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/openrouter/model-favorites .
All implementations use these shared paths and still read the old
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/config
file as a compatibility fallback when the provider-specific config is absent.
Important keys include MODEL, CONTEXT_TURNS, SESSION_DIR, ATTACHMENT_DIR,
MODEL_TEST_PROMPT, STARTUP_NOTICE, SESSION_AUTO_TITLE, SESSION_TITLE_MODEL,
SESSION_TITLE_MAX_WORDS, PROMPT_SESSION_NAME, WEB_SEARCH, WEB_SEARCH_ENGINE,
WEB_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS, WEB_SEARCH_MAX_USES, STREAM, AI_FILE_DOWNLOAD_MODE, STATUS_UPDATES, VOICE_INPUT_CMD,
VOICE_OUTPUT_CMD, TTS_CMD, VOICE_OUTPUT, MODEL_CACHE_FILE,
MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE, SEND_INPUT, THEME, CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES,
MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, and API_KEY_GPG_FILE.
.PP
SESSION_AUTO_TITLE defaults to 0. When enabled, SESSION_TITLE_MODEL is a
secondary model used only for a title and its corresponding managed filename.
The normal chat model remains MODEL; title generation never requests web search.
.PP
Session memory restores the latest complete JSON or legacy text snapshot, then
replays newer messages. Explicit memory edits and empty snapshots are preserved.
New snapshots use JSON so embedded newlines and role-looking text remain exact.
.SH RUNTIME COMMANDS
Interactive colon commands include :help, :rename TITLE, :turns, :branch N,
:web [on|off|status], :stream on|off, :ai-download MODE, :status on|off, :voice FILE, :speak on|off|last, :models,
:update-models, :select-model, :test-model MODEL, :config, :set KEY VALUE,
:memory, :edit-memory, :search TEXT, :search-all TEXT, :attach FILE, :editor,
and :credits.
.SH WEB SEARCH AND RESPONSE HANDLING
WEB_SEARCH=0 is the default. --web and :web on enable OpenRouter's current
openrouter:web_search server tool; :web shows its current state.
The deprecated web plugin and model :online suffix are not used automatically.
Searches may add provider charges. The result and use settings are bounds sent
to the provider, not a strict cost cap; native search may ignore some limits.
The request caps tool calls at five and total search results at fifteen. No local command execution is delegated to the model.
.PP
Sources remain human-readable in responses and session logs, including streamed
annotation events after text has ended. Available usage, response identifiers,
and annotations are also saved as system: openrouter-response: JSON metadata.
Session IDs are opaque and stable across title changes; titles and local paths
are not sent as request identifiers.
.PP
Streaming runs until [DONE], retains newline-only deltas and final usage, and
preserves partial output when stopped with ESC. API and transport errors are
reported as failures, never inserted into memory as assistant claims. Batch
commands return a nonzero status on failure. No automatic paid retries occur. If a reply has arrived but log or code-file
saving fails, its original text stays visible and the command reports failure.
Extracted code files use exclusive creation so previous replies are not overwritten.
.SH SEE ALSO
ttychatter.bash(1), ttychatter.ncurses(1)
